/T (Imagine a worker \(thread\) at a factory. When hired \(new state\), the worker waits for the task \(runnable state\). If the machine they need is occupied \(blocked\), they must wait. When the machine is free, they work, and finally, when the task is completed, they clock out \(terminated\).)
